# Do not add `/* /index.html 200`.
# Cloudflare Pages treats that splat as an infinite loop: the rewrite target
# `/index.html` is itself matched by `/*`, then extension stripping sends the
# request back through the same rule. A root 404.html also disables Pages'
# built-in SPA fallback, so the rule never produced HTTP 200 for deep links.
# Valid region and river URLs are real HTML files emitted by the Vite build.
# Anything else is this project's 404.html, served with status 404.
# /api/* is handled by Pages Functions and is not listed here.
